course: dictionary
lesson: 5405
title: A word from the African plains
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A kudu is a large African antelope, with grey-brown fur and thin white stripes. Antelope is a kind of animal, so the words around kudu tell you what it is.
explain: Look at this sentence: «In South Africa in the 1980s many kudu antelopes died on crowded farms.» The word antelopes sits right next to kudu, so kudu must be a kind of antelope.
explain: Some writers spell it differently. The sentence «The Giraffe, the Zebra, the Eland, the Koodoo (kudu) and the Hartebeest lived there» shows Koodoo in brackets with kudu after it, so the writer is telling you they are the same animal.
fact: A kudu is a large African antelope with grey-brown fur and thin white stripes.
fact: The males have long, spiral, twisted horns.
fact: There are two kinds of kudu: the greater kudu and the lesser kudu.
fact: Kudu eat leaves, and they are hunted by lions and leopards.
fact: Another spelling of kudu is «Koodoo».
exercise: «In South Africa many kudu antelopes lived on farms.» What is a kudu? | A kind of bird | A leafy tree | *A large African antelope | A type of farm fence
exercise: Kudu are hunted by which animals? | Penguins and seals | *Lions and leopards | Dolphins and whales | Rabbits and mice
exercise: The dictionary says there are two kinds of kudu. How many kinds are there? | One | Ten | Five | *Two
test: The sentence «The Giraffe, the Zebra, the Eland, the Koodoo (kudu) and the Hartebeest lived there» lists several names. What do these words name? | *Animals | Countries | Colours | Plants
test: The males have long, spiral, twisted horns. What shape are a male kudu's horns? | Soft and furry | *Long and twisted | Flat and square | Short and round
exam: In some places kudu horns are used as what? | *Musical horns | Roof tiles | Fences | Ploughs
